--TEST--
A `use` or a type naming a `Core` name nothing declares does not compile — `rule:core-api/reserved-namespace`
--FILE--
<?nvs
namespace Shop;

// `Core\Db` is a namespace with classes in it, so importing it compiles.
use Core\Db;
use Core\Db\DbError;
use Core\Json\Derive;
use Core\Nope;

class Order {
    public static function find(Core\Request $request, ?Core\Db\Missing $row): void {}
}
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0306]: `Core\Nope` does not resolve to any declaration
%A
error[E0303]: `Core\Db\Missing` is not declared
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
